louksna-linux-bridge (0.4.0-3) unstable; urgency=high

  * Add a local graphical status and diagnostics panel with a desktop launcher.
  * Display mTLS configuration and systemd state without auto-starting services.
  * Add python3-tk dependency and GUI packaging regression tests.
  * Add an explicit, fail-closed local mTLS provisioning command.
  * Generate separate CA, serverAuth and clientAuth identities; never reuse
    OpenSSH G23/G24/OWNER public keys as X.509 certificates.
  * Compute and validate all gateway pins using the runtime's exact schema.
  * Keep service installation disabled; provisioning never starts the service.
  * Report build evidence separately from G23/G24 certification and host tests.
  * Preserve fail-closed behavior and all existing runtime trust boundaries.

 -- Louksna Project <maintainers@louksna.invalid>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 03:15:00 +0000

louksna-linux-bridge (0.4.0-2) unstable; urgency=high

  * Do not enable or start the mTLS service during package installation.
  * Require explicit owner provisioning and validation of the mTLS config
    before the service can be activated.
  * Preserve fail-closed checks and all existing runtime trust boundaries.

 -- Louksna Project <maintainers@louksna.invalid>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0000

louksna-linux-bridge (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First Debian package for the Louksna Linux Bridge runtime.
  * Preserve loopback-only mTLS, bounded local transport, evidence ledger,
    fail-closed behavior and external G23/G24 authority.

 -- Louksna Project <maintainers@louksna.invalid>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 21:15:00 +0000
